What does this program print? (`Console.Write` does not add a new line.)

```csharp
static IEnumerable<int> Numbers()
{
    Console.Write("A");
    yield return 1;
    Console.Write("B");
    yield return 2;
    Console.Write("C");
}

foreach (int n in Numbers()) Console.Write(n);
Console.WriteLine();
```

What does this program print?

```csharp
IGreeter g = new Polite();
Console.WriteLine(g.Greet("Ama"));

interface IGreeter
{
    string Name { get; }
    string Greet(string who) => $"Hi {who}, I'm {Name}";
}

class Polite : IGreeter
{
    public string Name => "Polite";
    public string Greet(string who) => $"Good evening, {who}";
}
```

